# One issue per thread

**Owner law (2026-08-26):** An agent never verifies, fixes, or proves more than one named hole in the same chat. Chris copies each issue into its own thread.

An approved launch is one named task. Its required release-check failures may be repaired in parallel within that task under `approved-launch-release-blockers.mdc`; they are not separate hole tickets that need new owner prompts.

## Never

- Batch two board holes in one chat
- “Also do #7 while you’re in #6”
- Walk the other 18 “since I’m already in the file”
- Start a second hole because the first one is blocked

## Always

- This chat owns **only** the hole named in the paste
- After that one step, **stop**
- If a second hole appears, write it on the shared board and stop

## Example

```text
Paste: “VERIFY hole 6 — Remove Inquiries lie.”

❌ Recreate #6, then also check trial cap (#7) on the same Repair file.
✅ Recreate #6 only. Write PASS or NOT A PROBLEM. Stop.
```
